# Build-time public variables. Copy to `.env.production` for a deploy run from
# this machine; in CI the same names are set as Workers Builds *build*
# variables. Both are read by Vite at build time — an environment variable wins
# over a file of the same name.
#
# NOTHING SECRET MAY GO IN ONE. Anything Vite substitutes is in the bundle and
# is readable by anyone who opens the page.
#
# `.env*` is gitignored (this file excepted) because the repository is public.
# The PostHog token is not a credential — it ships in the bundle and only
# writes events — but a token committed here is a project every fork of this
# repository reports into, and the person who owns the project is not the
# person who forked it. Left unset, nothing reports, which is the correct
# behavior for a fork.

# Clerk's publishable key, `pk_test_…` or `pk_live_…`. See
# `src/account/accounts.ts`. `PUBLIC_` because Astro exposes nothing else to
# the browser. Not a secret — it names the instance and ships in the bundle —
# and still not committed, for the reason the PostHog token is not: a fork built from
# it would sign its visitors into somebody else's instance. Left unset, or set
# to anything that is not a real key, the build has no accounts: no badge, and
# account pages that say so.
#
# In Workers Builds it is a build variable of each environment: the production
# instance's `pk_live_…` in the Production build settings, the development
# instance's `pk_test_…` in Previews Base, beside each environment's own
# `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` on the Worker. For `pnpm dev`, the development key in
# `apps/game/.env.local`; the root `.env.local` is the Worker's alone. A
# `pk_live_…` key signs in on `inertialref.app` only; on any other host the
# build has no accounts.
#
# A production build reads `.env.local` too, so `pnpm run deploy:worker` from a
# machine set up for `pnpm dev` ships the `pk_test_…` key unless the production
# one is set in the environment, which wins over this file.
PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# PostHog: the project token, `phc_…`, and the ingest host of the project's
# region, `https://us.i.posthog.com`. `PUBLIC_` for the reason Clerk's key is.
# `src/telemetry/consent.ts` adds its own conditions on top: a production
# build, on `inertialref.app` (reported as `production`) or a Workers preview
# (`preview`), never against Global Privacy Control, never from a driven
# browser. So `pnpm dev`, `pnpm preview` and a LAN address report nothing
# whatever is set here. In Workers Builds both are build variables of the
# Production build settings and of Previews Base. The build also writes them
# into `dist/_headers` for crash reports (`vite.config.ts`).
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN=
PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
